obs wire.frame reads a session, not a raw payload, so serve rebuilds a committed session from the held payload and calls wire.frame — reusing the one proven framing path rather than inventing a second; identical payload bytes give an identical Sha256, so the served frame's content address equals the address asked for (content-preserving, sync converges)
obs serve refuses NotHeld before building a frame for an absent address; asserts deframe(served) equals the held payload and address_of(carried) equals the address served
obs four selftest blocks: serve answers only what is held (NotHeld for absent), content-preserving (far hand deposits under the same address), the whole local loop converges (far hand holding {bravo}, given the desk manifest of {alpha,bravo,charlie}, serves the 2 wanted and ends holding all 3), a tampered served frame refuses DigestMismatch and lands nothing (the far hand's deposit stays verify-before-trust)
obs catalog + manifest + serve now form a complete local content-addressed sync — advertise → compute wanted → serve → deposit verify-before-keep — the git have/want shape proven pure before any wire is strung
